WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.016 --> 00:00:04.520
- Hula is the language of the heart

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.530
and therefore the heartbeat
of the Hawaiian people.

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:10.113
(drum beating)

00:00:12.076 --> 00:00:15.335
And we tell our dancers,
everything needs to dance.

00:00:15.335 --> 00:00:19.502
Your hair, your toenail, your eyelashes,

00:00:21.194 --> 00:00:23.020
it needs to dance.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:27.103
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:00:31.841 --> 00:00:34.841
(upbeat drum music)

00:00:43.396 --> 00:00:46.335
Within three days the
competition tickets are sold out.

00:00:46.335 --> 00:00:48.668
Those tickets are like gold.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.982
They only bring the best of the best

00:00:52.982 --> 00:00:56.303
and so we're very honored
to be able to participate.

00:00:56.303 --> 00:01:00.199
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:01:00.199 --> 00:01:02.517
The most prestigious
part of Merrie Monarch

00:01:02.517 --> 00:01:04.345
is the Miss Aloha Hula competition,

00:01:04.345 --> 00:01:07.045
which is the women's solo competition.

00:01:07.045 --> 00:01:11.212
Twelve halaus are allowed to
choose their very best dancer.

00:01:13.933 --> 00:01:18.016
Our contestant this year
is Kayli Ka'iulani Carr.

00:01:19.485 --> 00:01:21.783
Kayli is a professional hula dancer

00:01:21.783 --> 00:01:25.308
and we chose her for
many different reasons.

00:01:25.308 --> 00:01:29.258
We wanted her to go, not just
a dancer, but as a person.

00:01:29.258 --> 00:01:33.175
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:35.926 --> 00:01:36.759
- One of my favorite parts

00:01:36.759 --> 00:01:37.995
about Merrie Monarch week is that

00:01:37.995 --> 00:01:41.378
we go to Kilauea to pay respects to Pele,

00:01:41.378 --> 00:01:45.461
who is the fire goddess,
the goddess of creation.

00:01:47.381 --> 00:01:49.828
And it really puts into perspective

00:01:49.828 --> 00:01:53.995
where you are in this world
and in this hula journey.

00:02:02.227 --> 00:02:05.170
I've wanted to be in Merrie Monarch

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:07.495
since I was a little kid.

00:02:07.495 --> 00:02:09.917
There was a lot of times
when I thought I would never,

00:02:09.917 --> 00:02:11.314
it would never happen for me

00:02:11.314 --> 00:02:14.227
but pretty much most of my hula journey

00:02:14.227 --> 00:02:18.394
has been working towards this
moment, which is tomorrow.

00:02:23.896 --> 00:02:27.287
Professionally, I've
been doing it since 2009.

00:02:27.287 --> 00:02:30.038
There is a difference between
dancing hula in a halau

00:02:30.038 --> 00:02:32.705
and dancing hula professionally.

00:02:34.147 --> 00:02:37.131
Dancing for the tourists
is like American Chinese

00:02:37.131 --> 00:02:40.748
and not the authentic Chinese food.

00:02:40.748 --> 00:02:44.304
- At hotels, here is what you'll see.

00:02:44.304 --> 00:02:47.837
Beautiful men and women,
brightly colored hair pieces

00:02:47.837 --> 00:02:50.524
and leis which are all plastic.

00:02:50.524 --> 00:02:53.683
But you won't see the skill,
you won't see the love

00:02:53.683 --> 00:02:56.456
that you would at the
Merrie Monarch Festival.

00:02:56.456 --> 00:02:59.491
- [Kayli] For Merrie Monarch
we practice every day for,

00:02:59.491 --> 00:03:01.635
I would say, three to four months.

00:03:01.635 --> 00:03:02.640
They're intense.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.020
- Can we try the end one more time.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.513
Why are you guys waiting?

00:03:06.513 --> 00:03:09.580
Invitation, you need one invitation?

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.111
Come on you guys, get your head game on.

00:03:12.111 --> 00:03:14.693
- The biggest misconception
about hula is that it's easy.

00:03:14.693 --> 00:03:17.093
All hula dancers, and you quote me on this,

00:03:17.093 --> 00:03:18.731
have bad knees, all of them.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:21.597
- [Ke'ano] So when you see
a beautiful hula dancer,

00:03:21.597 --> 00:03:24.694
that’s gliding across the
stage, she's hurting.

00:03:24.694 --> 00:03:26.540
She's hurting really bad

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:29.693
because nobody walks
around with bent knees.

00:03:29.693 --> 00:03:31.880
You know, six inches off the ground.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:34.970
- [Kayli] Blisters, you
get blisters on your feet.

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:38.007
- [Ke'ano] Every single part
of your body needs to work.

00:03:38.007 --> 00:03:40.616
You should be gasping for air.

00:03:40.616 --> 00:03:42.537
But you can't.

00:03:42.537 --> 00:03:46.008
You need to look exactly the
same as when you first started.

00:03:46.008 --> 00:03:48.312
- If you can bend your
knees and swirl your hips

00:03:48.312 --> 00:03:52.103
and have this upper body
carriage that's really upright

00:03:52.103 --> 00:03:53.768
but make it look effortless,

00:03:53.768 --> 00:03:55.775
that's a true hula dancer.

00:03:55.775 --> 00:03:56.608
- [Voiceover] Ladies and gentlemen,

00:03:56.608 --> 00:04:00.010
welcome to Miss Aloha Hula Competition.

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:02.843
Kayli Ka'iulani Carr.

00:04:03.698 --> 00:04:05.931
- [Kayli] If I gave the
performance of a lifetime,

00:04:05.931 --> 00:04:09.145
if I gave everything I had
to that one performance,

00:04:09.145 --> 00:04:11.153
those 14 minutes up there, just me,

00:04:11.153 --> 00:04:12.570
I've already won.

00:04:13.606 --> 00:04:16.606
(audience cheering)

00:04:26.168 --> 00:04:27.754
You're just the vessel
for all of these people

00:04:27.754 --> 00:04:28.843
that came before you.

00:04:28.843 --> 00:04:30.372
For all of the knowledge that you have

00:04:30.372 --> 00:04:32.122
and it's your responsibility
to share that,

00:04:32.122 --> 00:04:35.372
it's your responsibility to perpetuate.

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:41.105
But, it would be so nice to hear my name

00:04:41.105 --> 00:04:42.792
being called.

00:04:42.792 --> 00:04:43.840
- And now ladies and gentlemen,

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:45.840
Miss Aloha Hula for 2016

00:04:46.734 --> 00:04:49.204
Kayli Ka'iulani Carr.

00:04:49.204 --> 00:04:52.204
(audience cheering)

00:04:54.612 --> 00:04:55.925
- [Kayli] You know, I don't dance hula

00:04:55.925 --> 00:04:57.989
just to be a Miss Aloha Hula.

00:04:57.989 --> 00:04:59.570
I do it because,

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.625
just because I love it.

00:05:01.625 --> 00:05:04.625
And I can't explain to you why I do.

00:05:06.403 --> 00:05:10.153
I think it's something
you're just born with.

